  "title": "Lise Meitner",
  "summary": "Lise Meitner was born in Vienna on 7 November 1878 and died in Cambridge, England, on 27 October 1968. She worked at the Kaiser Wilhelm Institute for Chemistry in Berlin, leading its Radiophysics sub-department, until she left Germany in 1938. In January 1939 she and Otto Frisch gave the physical explanation of the fission Hahn and Straßmann found.",
